2|0@guns^1439006561#ctvlz4t:Small_Simple_Ships$:I've dealt with many of the MVP rifles. They are decent. They are not the best at anything. You can find much better shooting rifles for the same price. HOWEVER - if you really like the look of them, and don't need a sub-MOA tackdriver, and just want it because you want it - I say go for it. I've noticed that about half of the ones I've played with have really rough-moving bolts. Not rough as it "it will break itself in" rough, but more like "this was poorly designed and machined and it will always be rough" rough. The ability to take AR mags is sort of weird because you are basically getting a less-accurate, slower shooting, crappier all around shooting experience than just using the mags in an actual AR.
